[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2077786504","pull_request_review_id":2822021260,"id":2077786504,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc572IGI","diff_hunk":"@@ -3095,6 +3095,10 @@\n \t\t<member name=\"rendering/reflections/sky_reflections/texture_array_reflections.mobile\" type=\"bool\" setter=\"\" getter=\"\" default=\"false\">\n \t\t\tLower-end override for [member rendering/reflections/sky_reflections/texture_array_reflections] on mobile devices, due to performance concerns or driver support.\n \t\t</member>\n+\t\t<member name=\"rendering/reflections/specular_occlusion/enabled\" type=\"bool\" setter=\"\" getter=\"\" default=\"true\">\n+\t\t\tIf [code]true[/code], reduces reflections based on ambient light.\n+\t\t\t[b]Note:[/b] When [member LightmapGI.directional] is set to [code]true[/code], this feature is disabled.","path":"doc/classes/ProjectSettings.xml","commit_id":"56730d0cb2e4fd06c0ef23c7e44d8e9e8e64edf0","original_commit_id":"7df3ce1fc638fc261dcc5e4f54289d3ae8b7aba6","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Out of curiosity, why is that the case? I can't see any references to directional lightmaps (or `sh`) in the PR's diff.\r\n\r\nAlso, I believe that even if this was done, SSAO would still be affected by this (as SSAO can't know whether direct or indirect light was baked in the lightmap, regardless of whether it's directional or not). As a result, SSAO treats lightmaps as pure ambient (indirect) light. It will always darken lightmaps as if SSAO Light Affect was always 1.0, even if it's a lower value.\r\n\r\nQuoting from the PR description:\r\n\r\n> This PR does a slightly better job at maintaining reflections that shouldn't be occluded, occluding reflections only once the ambient lighting crosses a certain threshold.\r\n\r\nWe could address this caveat of SSAO by treating lightmap brightness above a certain value as direct light, and making it take SSAO Light Affect into account. For example, if lightmap value is above 0.5, you could treat values above 0.5 as direct light for the purposes of SSAO.","created_at":"2025-05-07T14:35:51Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T14:39:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#discussion_r2077786504","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106145","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2077786504"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#discussion_r2077786504"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106145"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2077786504/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":3100,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2077790302","pull_request_review_id":2822021260,"id":2077790302,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc572JBe","diff_hunk":"@@ -1382,6 +1382,11 @@ MaterialStorage::MaterialStorage() {\n \t\t}\n \t\tactions.render_mode_defines[\"fog_disabled\"] = \"#define FOG_DISABLED\\n\";\n \n+\t\tbool specular_occlusion = GLOBAL_GET(\"rendering/reflections/specular_occlusion/enabled\");\n+\t\tif (specular_occlusion) {\n+\t\t\tactions.render_mode_defines[\"specular_occlusion\"] = \"#define USE_SPECULAR_OCCLUSION\\n\";\n+\t\t}","path":"drivers/gles3/storage/material_storage.cpp","commit_id":"56730d0cb2e4fd06c0ef23c7e44d8e9e8e64edf0","original_commit_id":"7df3ce1fc638fc261dcc5e4f54289d3ae8b7aba6","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Should the render mode be flipped to `specular_occlusion_disabled`? Right now, custom shaders that don't specify any render mode will look different to a BaseMaterial3D in its default configuration, since the BaseMaterial3D will use specular occlusion but not the custom shader.\r\n\r\nDoing so would also match the high-level API in BaseMaterial3D.","created_at":"2025-05-07T14:37:03Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T14:37:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#discussion_r2077790302","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106145","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2077790302"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#discussion_r2077790302"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106145"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2077790302/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1385,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":1388,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2077901023","pull_request_review_id":2822230090,"id":2077901023,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc572kDf","diff_hunk":"@@ -3095,6 +3095,10 @@\n \t\t<member name=\"rendering/reflections/sky_reflections/texture_array_reflections.mobile\" type=\"bool\" setter=\"\" getter=\"\" default=\"false\">\n \t\t\tLower-end override for [member rendering/reflections/sky_reflections/texture_array_reflections] on mobile devices, due to performance concerns or driver support.\n \t\t</member>\n+\t\t<member name=\"rendering/reflections/specular_occlusion/enabled\" type=\"bool\" setter=\"\" getter=\"\" default=\"true\">\n+\t\t\tIf [code]true[/code], reduces reflections based on ambient light.\n+\t\t\t[b]Note:[/b] When [member LightmapGI.directional] is set to [code]true[/code], this feature is disabled.","path":"doc/classes/ProjectSettings.xml","commit_id":"56730d0cb2e4fd06c0ef23c7e44d8e9e8e64edf0","original_commit_id":"7df3ce1fc638fc261dcc5e4f54289d3ae8b7aba6","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Ah yeah, that line is irrelevant in my pr, just something I forgot to edit out of the original PR. :)\r\n\r\n> We could address this caveat of SSAO\r\n\r\nWhat I'm referencing in that quote is not an issue caused by SSAO, it's just kind of a caveat of this technique as a whole and I don't think it can be mitigated (easily). Doing something like baking scene-wide bent normals would probably improve this from my understanding (And I believe this is what Unreal does), but that's a little out of scope for me. I think this approach still gets us 90% of the way there for a fraction of the cost though.\r\n\r\nWhat would hugely improve specular occlusion based on SSAO though would be an improved SSAO technique that captures the variety in depth better.","created_at":"2025-05-07T15:17:24Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T15:17:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#discussion_r2077901023","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106145","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2077901023"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106145#discussion_r2077901023"},"pull_reques